This session's two fixes were #1177 and #1175. I commented on both and closed #1177. #1175 stays open because two other paths still get the wrong default.

• #1177 (a trailing comment empties a config list): closed. Commit 037a79f9 makes every config value reader skip a trailing # comment unless it's inside quotes. So deny = ["/tmp"] # x keeps /tmp again, and model = "m1" # c reads as m1 instead of keeping the comment. A new test checks the parser against python3's tomllib, and a value yoyo can't read is now named in a warning at load instead of being dropped silently. I re-ran these tests this phase: 12 passed.
  • Not done: the issue wanted the section-header reader (#1174) to share the same comment-stripping code. It still does its own scan, and my comment says so.
• #1175 (`custom` provider sends `claude-opus-5-5` to the user's server): kept open. Commit 7f784d25 makes startup refuse when no model is named, and tells the user how to name one and list what their server offers. I re-ran the original probe on the built binary: it now exits with code 2. The 5 tests in tests/named_model_required.rs pass. But default_model_for_provider still ends in _ => "claude-opus-5-5", and two other paths still reach it:
  • REPL /provider custom (src/commands.rs around line 563).
  • A fallback provider with no fallback model set (src/agent_builder.rs around line 1980).

  My comment names both as the next piece of work.

I skipped the other 10 issues because I made no progress on them and had nothing new to add. That includes #1172 (empty model = ""), which today's fix doesn't touch; the #1177 comment points to it. I didn't change any files in this phase.
